      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:xfa6yu'
    female|a||Two years later, twenty-one percent.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 2760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:15712kw'
    'female|a||The obvious answer is the whole fall: twelve percentage points.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ntipeh'
    'female|a||But 2014 brought more than Medicaid: subsidised private plans, a rule that everyone be insured, and jobs coming back, in nearly every state.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:hdpizb'
    'female|a||So look at the states that did not expand: thirty-seven percent uninsured in 2013, twenty-nine in 2015.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:h3fja2'
    female|a||They fell eight points with no expansion at all, from everything else that 2014 brought.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1iac1ru'
    female|a||If the expansion states had gone through the same eight-point fall, they would have landed at twenty-five.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:188er5m'
    female|a||They landed at twenty-one. The four points between the two are the estimate of what expanding did.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10bj1l8'
    'female|a||Written out, it is the change in the expansion states minus the change in the others: a difference in differences.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10hweg3'
    'female|a||Minus twelve, less minus eight, leaves minus four: four points fewer uninsured.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ul8821'
    'female|a||The two groups never started level: the others were four points worse off in 2013, and the method doesn''t mind.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:ujjbe0'
    female|a||A steady gap between groups cancels out in the subtraction; only the changes count.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1w0yw7r'
    female|a||Try new numbers. Suppose the states that did not expand had fallen only from 37 to 33, while the expansion states still went from 33 to 21. What is the estimate?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 14760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1d36n6k'
    'female|a||Minus eight: the expansion states fell twelve, the others four, and the estimate is the difference between those two falls.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||But every step of that rested on one dashed line, and nobody has ever seen it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6240
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Four points fewer uninsured: that answer rests on a guess, that without expanding, those states would have fallen just as far as the others.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Call living in an expansion state D equals one, and write Y-zero for the uninsured rate a group would have had without expanding.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:dkdv9y'
    'female|a||For the states that did not expand, the change in Y-zero is simply what happened: their fall of eight.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1dp7phl'
    female|a||For the expansion states, Y-zero in 2015 never happened. It is the dashed line, with its question mark.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10rqsrt'
    'female|a||Parallel trends says those two changes are equal on average. Not the levels: the changes.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:dau70f'
    'female|a||If the assumption fails, the estimate is the true average effect on the expansion states, the ATT, plus a bias, B: the gap between the two untreated trends.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:v7e7kw'
    'female|a||Right now the dashed line falls eight points, so the bias is zero, and the true effect equals the estimate: minus four.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1p42qjx'
    'female|a||Watch the dashed line fall faster: the true effect shrinks and the bias grows, while the estimate stays at minus four.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1mpuep3'
    female|a||At an eleven-point fall, the true effect is only minus one. The other three points are bias, and the estimate still says minus four.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||And nothing in the 2013 and 2015 numbers can tell those two worlds apart: the data are the same in both.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1s7vzvo'
    female|a||So researchers look back, to the years before anyone expanded.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:pcxejc'
    female|a||Here both groups drift down half a point a year, side by side, from 2010 to 2013.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1sa1qdf'
    female|a||But the assumption is about 2015, after the expansion, and no earlier year can reach that dashed line.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1o48cu1'
    female|a||From 2010 to 2013 the two groups moved in parallel. What does that show?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1pkl0gw'
    female|a||It shows the groups moved together before 2014. That rules out some bad stories, but the assumption is about the years after.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9440
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Parallel lines before a policy are a failed attempt to refute the assumption, never a proof of it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||And real data are noisy in every year, so even the past can hide a slow drift between the groups.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10ix82a'
    female|a||Fewer uninsured is one thing. Did expanding Medicaid keep people alive? Sarah Miller, Norman Johnson and Laura Wherry used this design to ask.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10840
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||They took more than half a million low-income or less-educated Americans aged fifty-five to sixty-four from a large Census survey, and linked them to death records up to 2017.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:u2afy1'
    female|a||Each dot is the gap in yearly deaths per thousand between expansion and non-expansion states, measured against 2013, with its ninety-five percent range. Before 2014 they hover around zero.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 14720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:3uw6q3'
    'female|a||After, the gap opens year by year: almost one death fewer per thousand in 2014, about two fewer by 2017.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1i6s5qh'
    'female|a||Their summary estimate: one point three fewer deaths per thousand a year, about nine percent, with a range from about point three to two point three.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1m0cci8'
    female|a||That is the effect of expanding on the whole group, most of whom never enrolled, so if it worked only through those who gained Medicaid, their own effect was about seven times larger.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1i4fmx5'
    'female|a||But the early bars are wide: a drift of a fifth of a death per thousand a year fits inside every one, and carried forward could explain a third to three-quarters of the estimate.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:q4olyz'
    'female|a||And the usual test would not catch it: Jonathan Roth showed in 2022 that pre-trend tests in published studies often miss drifts big enough to matter, so passing one proves little.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:g22tr8'
    female|a||So what story could break parallel trends here?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1tqstts'
    female|a||Expansion states were not a random half. Their low-income adults were a little better off, and fewer of them were uninsured to begin with.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lcs6f7'
    female|a||So anything else that moved their death rates from 2014, a faster recovery, a different turn in the overdose crisis, would be booked as Medicaid.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:xa6hnd'
    'female|a||The authors looked where such a shock would show but Medicaid could not: people already sixty-five, on Medicare. Their gap stayed flat.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:26rwwv'
    female|a||Not everyone is persuaded. Bernard Black and colleagues, working with county death counts, found no statistically clear fall, and showed that designs like theirs can only see very large effects.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:hbz15e'
    'female|a||What separates the two readings is precision and checks: records on each person who could gain Medicaid, the flat gap for the over-sixty-fives, and a fall in deaths from disease rather than accidents.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1dfpjm4'
    female|a||Oregon's 2008 lottery, which offered Medicaid by chance to some of about ninety thousand applicants, needs no such assumption. But it was too small and too short to settle deaths.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:8tkfgl'
    female|a||One new case. A study compares hospital deaths in states that raised nurse staffing in 2016 with states that did not. Which finding would worry you most?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11hrcy1'
    female|a||The trauma centres arrive with the policy, in the same states, so they move the untreated path itself, and the double difference books them as the staffing effect.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10320
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||So how much of the fall was Medicaid's? The double difference answers by taking the others' change from the expansion states' change.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||That answer is causal only if, untreated, both groups would have moved alike: a claim about a line no one ever saw.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2qrnsl'
    female|a||Flat years before can refute that claim but never prove it, so a good study argues for the line with every check it can find.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11jte1b'
    female|a||Work out how far the others fell first, then take that from the expansion states' fall.:
